      "proof_or_statement_rewrites": [],
      "options": [
        "set_option autoImplicit false",
        "set_option warningAsError true"
      ],
      "module_doc_added": "/-!\n# Ordinary input and singleton output for finite stack packages\n\nThe wrapper fixes a native machine before the raw input is supplied. It uses\nthe package's work alphabet, its exact supported starting control, and an\ninjective nonblank letter map. Finiteness of the work alphabet requires finite\nalphabets at every source stack index.\n\n`runInTime` consumes an actual bounded encoded native run and a complete\n`TM2to1.TrCfg` relation to `haltList tm [answer]`. It composes the paid input\nprelude with the supplied run and one output write, reaching the whole singleton\noutput tape with blank tails. Its bound is `preludeSteps raw + B + 1`;\n`nextNoneRun` pays one additional step to observe outer `none`. The native\nevaluation theorem follows from this complete endpoint.\n-/\n"
    },
    {
      "owner": "Applications/Resources/TuringSimulation/PrintMove.lean",
      "output": {
        "path": "/workspace/scratch/ae71b485b114/work/integration147-drafts/Applications/Resources/TuringSimulation/PrintMove.lean",
        "bytes": 33332,
        "sha256": "ce762c2b07cd1414f1e47b0dfef74d558a808a213db0d71e5d970fe1516c9fe4",
        "mode": "0644"
      },
      "imports_added": [
        "Mathlib.Computability.TuringMachine.PostTuringMachine",
        "Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Sum",
        "Mathlib.Tactic.DeriveFintype",
        "Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card",
        "Mathlib.Data.Int.Interval",
        "Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic"
      ],
      "body_blocks": [
        "printmove_adapter",
        "printmove_trace"
      ],
      "proof_or_statement_rewrites": [],
      "options": [
        "set_option autoImplicit false",
        "set_option warningAsError true"
      ],
      "module_doc_added": "/-!\n# Native simulation by print-and-move transitions\n\nEach target action writes a symbol and moves exactly one square. The adapter\npreserves the native alphabet, supplied start and complete physical tape at\nnormal control boundaries. A native move costs one target action; a native\nwrite costs two, with its rightward excursion and return included. A final\ndecision action reaches an accepting or rejecting control and moves the tape\nright. For a stopped native endpoint with a Boolean output, a native bound `B`\ntherefore yields a deciding bound `2 * B + 1`.\n\nThe trace API observes every actual target prefix, including write excursions\nand the final decision. It bounds the input-inclusive visited interval by\n`max N 1 + U` for target time `U`. This interval observation does not assert\nbounded support for an arbitrary initial tape.\n-/\n"
    },
    {
      "owner": "Applications/Resources/TuringSimulation/PolynomialDeciderPrintMove.lean",
      "output": {
        "path": "/workspace/scratch/ae71b485b114/work/integration147-drafts/Applications/Resources/TuringSimulation/PolynomialDeciderPrintMove.lean",
        "bytes": 7587,
        "sha256": "eb4519ab3ca559d9f740a8c963367428f2ae7c5dbefa6e198eb2bbb62c2ecb7f",
        "mode": "0644"
      },
      "imports_added": [
        "Applications.Resources.TuringSimulation.PolynomialDecider",
        "Applications.Resources.TuringSimulation.PrintMove"
      ],
      "body_blocks": [
        "polynomial_consumer"
      ],
      "proof_or_statement_rewrites": [],
      "options": [
        "set_option autoImplicit false",
        "set_option warningAsError true"
      ],
      "module_doc_added": "/-!\n# Print-and-move realization of native polynomial Boolean deciders\n\nThe construction fixes finite target control before the input, preserving the\nnative decider's blank, supplied start and injective nonblank Boolean letters.\nIts time polynomial evaluates to `2 * d.time.eval N + 1`. The run theorem\nretains actual native and target witnesses and the complete final tape; the\nspace theorem observes every target prefix on the literal input length.\n\n`printMoveMachine` uses supplied decidable alphabet equality. The classical variant\nprovides a noncomputable finite machine from the same native contract.\n-/\n"
    },
